{#
compose/_undo_toast.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Cancelling a send from the dock: say so, and put the window back exactly as it
was — recipients, subject, body and attachments included.

`replace` rather than `append`, and `only` rather than an inherited context:

  • The window's own root element IS <turbo-frame id="compose_dock">, so
    appending it *into* that frame nested a frame inside itself and left the
    previous (emptied) one wrapping it. Replacing swaps the frame for the new
    one, which is what _inline_undo.stream.html.twig does for its frame.

  • Without `only`, the include inherited whatever the caller happened to have
    and silently did without the rest. `pickerIntegrations` was the one it did
    without, which under strict_variables made the whole undo a 500 — and the
    cancel had already been flushed by then, so the send was called off while
    the window it belonged to never came back.

Variables: form, message, ctx, pickerIntegrations
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type: 'info',
            message: 'toast.send_cancelled'|trans,
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

<turbo-stream action="replace" target="{{ ctx.frame }}">
    <template>
        {% include 'compose/_window.html.twig' with {
            form:    form,
            message: message,
            ctx:     ctx,
            pickerIntegrations: pickerIntegrations,
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
